    "mission": "Breakthrough partners with people to build connections, develop skills, and open doors of opportunity. Breakthrough envisions a safe, stable, engaged Garfield Park where success is the norm and everyone thrives.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Breakthrough is intentionally located in the East Garfield Park neighborhood, a hard-working west-side community with 180 acres of parkland, active block clubs, generations-old churches, and longstanding residents committed to the well-being of the community. The community has faced historical disinvestment over the last 60 years. East Garfield Park is predominantly Black (84%), and 72% of residents do not have a college degree. Over 43% of residents live below the poverty level, and over 17% of residents are unemployed (CMAP 2024). Life expectancy in East Garfield Park is 68, which is 20 years less than in the City-Wide (Chicago Health Atlas). \n\nIn a commitment to cultivating relationships built on dignity and respect, Breakthrough and East Garfield Park residents are working together to catalyze transformation within East Garfield Park, where success becomes the norm and everyone thrives. Breakthrough delivers a continuum of services that support individuals and families in reaching their full potential. Funds from Knight Impact Partners will help sustain and strengthen programming across Breakthrough\u2019s five key focus areas:\n\nHousing\nBreakthrough addresses housing instability through a continuum of services, including daytime support, emergency shelter, transitional housing for 60 adults, and 43 units of permanent supportive housing for single adults. Additionally, 11 families receive case management in permanent supportive housing. Participants access comprehensive wraparound services such as healthcare, food, employment support, and emergency assistance. In 2026, Breakthrough will expand its housing efforts with the opening of The Turning Point, a 14-unit building designed to support families facing housing insecurity.\n\nHealth & Wellness\nBreakthrough\u2019s health and wellness initiatives promote holistic well-being. Behavioral Health services provide therapy and mental health support for all ages. The Fresh Market, a client-choice food pantry, offers fresh groceries three times weekly and connects visitors with SNAP benefits. In partnership with Lawndale Christian Health Center, Breakthrough provides on-site medical care. A community fitness center further promotes physical health and wellness.\n\nEconomic Opportunity\nBreakthrough\u2019s Economic Opportunity programs empower individuals through five key services: workforce training, financial coaching, income support access, housing education, and small business development.\n\nEducation & Youth Development\nBreakthrough operates five year-round programs that support children and youth from early childhood through young adulthood:\nBreakthrough Beginners: A full-day early childhood education for children ages 2\u20135.\nNettie Bailey Student Achievement Program: After-school and summer programming for K\u20138 students.\nLondon Johnson Arts & Technology Academy: STEAM-based learning focused on arts and tech.\nSports & Fitness Academy: Athletics programs that promote personal growth and teamwork.\nBreakthrough Beyond: High school mentorship and college access guidance with an emphasis on engaging opportunity youth.\n\nViolence Prevention\nTo interrupt cycles of violence, Breakthrough provides street outreach, case management, and victim services for individuals impacted by gun violence. The program also hosts community safe-space events that reduce retaliatory violence and reclaim public spaces for peace and healing.",
