    "volunteers": "2,000 annually",
    "mission": "Transforming Communities. One Child at a Time.\n\nInterrupting cycles of poverty, disinvestment, and hopelessness takes more than good intentions\u2014it takes a long-term, holistic commitment. At By The Hand, transformation is happening every day\u2014story by story, life by life, neighborhood by neighborhood.\n\nAcross some of Chicago\u2019s most under-resourced communities, our students are being cared for and empowered\u2014mind, body, and soul. Through access to critical human services, healthcare, educational pathways, and community-driven development, we are building a future where every child can thrive.\n\nOUR VISION \nHelping children who live in under-resourced neighborhoods have abundant life.\n\nOUR MISSION \nBy The Hand is a Christ-centered, after-school program that takes kids by the hand and walks with them from kindergarten through college, loving and nurturing them\u2014mind, body and soul. We love and nurture our kids through offering the following services:\n- Technology-based reading\n- Academic support and tutoring\n- Enrichment activities: field trips, music and dance/art classes, media and digital arts\n- Eye and dental care\n- Hot, nutritious meals\n- Counseling and social-emotional learning curriculum\n- Mentoring and discipleship \n- College and career preparation, scholarships and post-secondary support \n- Care for the entire family through our Crisis and Compassion department",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "By The Hand Club For Kids is a faith-based, after-school organization that serves more than 2,100 students across six locations in Chicago. We are intentionally located in neighborhoods facing the highest levels of economic hardship, as identified by the U.S. Census and the Area Deprivation Index. To ensure we reach the students with the greatest need, we partner directly with public schools within a mile of each site. These schools verify student income status using federal guidelines such as eligibility for free or reduced-price lunch. Across our partner schools, 85\u201399% of students are identified as low income, with an average of 95%. By embedding our services in these communities, we ensure consistent access to students and families who face the most significant barriers to opportunity.\n\nRooted in our mission to help children experience abundant life\u2014mind, body, and soul\u2014we provide holistic support beginning in early elementary school and continuing through young adulthood. Our programs offer academic tutoring, reading intervention, meals, health services, mentorship, spiritual development, and a continuum of support through high school graduation and beyond.\n\nAs students advance, they transition into our College and Career Readiness Program, which prepares them to succeed in college, career, and life. This program begins with personalized academic support, counseling through key transitions, and regular academic check-ins. Students are exposed to real-world opportunities through college visits, career talks, and entrepreneurship experiences at our youth-led produce market, Austin Harvest, and hydroponic farm, Bowen Harvest.\n\nAs seniors approach graduation, we provide hands-on support with FAFSA completion, financial literacy, college and trade school applications, and post-secondary decision-making. Each senior is paired with a mentor through our NXT Steps program, walking with them through their first year after high school. Students receive scholarships, campus visits to monitor progress, and support with essentials like r\u00e9sum\u00e9 development, internships, and even transportation to college. Whether it\u2019s moving a student into their dorm or connecting them to a first job, we remain a steady source of encouragement and accountability.\n\nThis school year, our College and Career Readiness Program will serve 350 high school students and 125 alumni enrolled in college, trade school, the military, or the workforce. New initiatives include ONU+, a partnership with Olivet Nazarene University that allows students to pursue college while staying rooted in their communities and connected to By The Hand support.\n\nThis work directly aligns with our organizational goal: that every student we serve would experience abundant life. We measure success through growth in three dimensions:\n\nMind: Students maintain a B average or higher, complete post-secondary education or training, gain meaningful work and volunteer experience, and give back to their communities.\n\nBody: Students lead active, healthy lifestyles, avoid risky behaviors, demonstrate self-efficacy, and participate in leadership or advocacy.\n\nSoul: Students develop a personal faith, apply it to life decisions, lead with integrity and compassion, and engage in their church or youth community.\n\nBy addressing academic achievement, health and wellness, workforce readiness, and spiritual development students are equipped to walk through those doors and thrive.",
