    "leader_email": "kminer@ccachicago.org",
    "full_time_staff": "23",
    "part_time_staff": "0",
    "volunteers": "111",
    "mission": "Civic Consulting Alliance's mission is to make the Chicago region a great place for everyone to live in and work. We are a nonprofit organization bringing together collaborative investments to get big things done for Chicago. We provide pro bono consulting services that are amplified by the capacity and expertise of our corporate partners. Together, we work to advance systems-level solutions that untangle interconnected issues like economic and educational opportunity gaps, violence, and injustice that affect residents. \n\nWe build meaningful connections with government, social impact and corporate leaders and provide the capacity needed to advance projects that reshape our region to be more just, equitable, and resilient. Our clients value this effective model as a neutral party that allows for collaborative, intricate, and expedient work. We leverage our institutional knowledge, cross-sector relationships, as well as data, research, and analysis, to inform clients\u2019 decisions and build sustainable solutions. \n\nSince Mayor Harold Washington first convened a private-sector budget task force in 1985, we have served as an invaluable component of the Chicago region\u2019s civic infrastructure. Every dollar invested in our mission is multiplied fivefold, providing an average of $20 million in pro bono consulting services annually.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Thank you for considering a grant to Civic Consulting Alliance\u2019s Economic Vitality Platform in recognition of the value that Civic Consulting Alliance brings to this critical moment in working with the City of Chicago on the 5-Year Homelessness Plan. \n\nOur Economic Vitality Platform:\n\nCivic Consulting Alliance\u2019s work on the 5-year Homelessness Plan with the City falls within our Economic Vitality platform, where we are committed to increasing the vitality of our region and reducing disparity between neighborhoods. We invest in building an inclusive and equitable economy that contributes to the long-term vitality of the Chicago region. We focus on:\n\n--->Inclusive regional economic growth\n--->Equitable investment across communities\n--->Individual opportunity & prosperity\n--->Responsive and efficient institution\n\n5-year Homelessness Plan Project:\n\nThe Mayor\u2019s Office appointed Sendy Soto to be the City\u2019s first Chief Homelessness Officer. One of her main priorities is to develop a new 5-year plan to reduce homelessness in Chicago. The City\u2019s previous plan was completed in 2012 under the Emanuel Administration. Soto has launched an extensive stakeholder engagement exercise as part of the plan\u2019s development that will take place between October 2024 and February of 2025. Her team will then develop a draft of the plan between March and April of 2025, to be followed by a round of public comment. In addition, Soto has convened an inter-agency task force on homelessness to understand current budgets and initiatives to address this urgent issue and complement the external engagement exercise. \n\nCivic Consulting Alliance is and will be involved in the plan development process, providing critical thought partnership, project management support, and research and analysis. We are well-positioned to guide the collaboration this project requires, given our deep relationships of trust as a neutral party with local government and various other stakeholders.",
    "amount_requested": 50000.0,
    "grant_amount_awarded": 50000.0,
    "grant_type": "Systems Building",
