    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "With a mission to serve and catalyze our community to end homelessness, one person at a time, we are leading our region's efforts to attain functional zero status by making homelessness rare, brief and non-recurring. Headquartered in Evanston, we meet the needs of those living across Chicago\u2019s northern suburbs through a two-fold approach: first, we provide housing, shelter, homelessness prevention, and supportive services. We also address the systemic and structural causes of homelessness and racial inequality through the advocacy coalition that we formed and lead, Joining Forces for Affordable Housing. Our advocacy efforts started locally in Evanston, but have now expanded throughout Chicago\u2019s northern suburbs into Lake County.\n\nSince the start of the COVID-19 pandemic, we have doubled the number of people served across our programs to nearly 5,000 across 52 Chicagoland communities. With the partnership of Knight Impact Partners and other supporters, we seek to sustain and grow our services to meet the growing demand for services and affordable housing advocacy in our community.",
