    "id": "27",
    "name": "Erie Family Health Foundation",
    "address": "1701 W. Superior",
    "address_line2": "Third Floor",
    "city": "Chicago",
    "state": "IL",
    "postal_code": "60622",
    "website": "www.eriefamilyhealth.org",
    "email": "",
    "phone": "312-432-7463",
    "year_founded": "1957",
    "tax_id": "81-4172423",
    "contact_first_name": "Melissa",
    "contact_last_name": "Hilton",
    "contact_title": "VP of Development and Executive Director, Erie Family Health Foundation",
    "contact_email": "mhilton@eriefamilyhealth.org",
    "leader_first_name": "Sandra",
    "leader_last_name": "Del Toro",
    "leader_title": "Senior Director of Development",
    "leader_email": "sdeltoro@eriefamilyhealth.org",
    "full_time_staff": "721",
    "part_time_staff": "104",
    "volunteers": "8",
    "mission": "Erie Family Health Centers (Erie) is a healthcare home to more than 95,000 patients, mostly low-income, who are served in the Chicago area at thirteen locations. Erie\u2019s steadfast commitment to helping patients in need is reflected in our mission statement: Motivated by the belief that healthcare is a human right, we provide high quality, affordable care to support healthier people, families and communities. Erie serves patients experiencing poverty, and nearly 88% of Erie patients are either Medicaid recipients or have no health insurance. Erie\u2019s patient population reflects the service areas where our health centers are located, and 66% of our patients are Latino and 10% are Black. \nIn 2017, Erie created the Erie Family Health Foundation (EFHF) as a supporting foundation to complement its patient-majority governing board. Our Foundation\u2019s board members are focused on building philanthropic relationships and securing investments in essential programs and services that would otherwise be unavailable to Erie patients. The board leverages their connections, networks and resources to advance fundraising efforts with individuals, events, foundations and corporations. Every dollar donated to EFHF is directed to programs and services at Erie Family Health Centers.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Primary Focus: Erie takes a holistic approach to reproductive health equity that supports patients across the lifespan and promotes healthy pregnancies and a healthy start in life for babies.  As the activities below reflect, the proposed project will: (1) provide comprehensive reproductive health services to our patient population; (2) provide holistic maternal health and supportive services to Erie\u2019s more than 4,000 pregnant patients and their children and; (3) support Erie\u2019s ability to respond to emerging threats and opportunities in the healthcare landscape in the development of its maternal health programs. \nTarget Population: Erie is particularly skilled at addressing health disparities and responding to the special health needs of women, who represent the majority of our patients  (61%). Ninety percent of Erie\u2019s patients subsist at income levels below 200% of the federal poverty level. Erie also serves predominantly people of color; 66% of patients are Latino, 10% are Black, and 49% are best served in a language other than English, with 97 unique languages spoken among our patient population.  \n\nErie has deep expertise caring for pregnant and postpartum patients and ensuring that they achieve the best possible outcomes. In calendar year 2023, Erie served more than 24,000 female patients ages 18-44 and a total of 5,252 prenatal care patients. Approximately 2,300 prenatal patients had babies delivered by Erie providers during 2023, ranking Erie the highest in the state and in the top 1% nationwide for the number of babies delivered. In FY24, Erie's OB/GYN physicians served patients through over 34,707 visits and our Certified Nurse Midwives served patients through an additional 24,494 visits.  In addition to expert medical care, Erie has dedicated programming for reproductive health, including family planning for birthing age adults, case management through the prenatal and postpartum period, dental care, behavioral health services and more throughout pregnancy. Among Erie\u2019s pregnant patients, 63.7% identified as Latino and 7.4% identified as Black. A significant percentage identified as mixed race or chose not to disclose. \n\nKey Activities: In addition to exploring enhancements to our service model, Erie will provide health care as well as a suite of robust supportive services that have enabled us to achieve leading outcomes for patients, including:\n1)\tVerification of Pregnancy: Erie will offer verification of pregnancy and options counseling for both patients and community members and assess and link patients to appropriate services. We will continue to promote these services as well as the additional services described below throughout the service area.\n2)\tChronic Disease management: Erie will provide programs and services to help pregnant patients manage chronic conditions such as diabetes and hypertension through bilingual health education and hands-on instruction, development of self-management plans, and  outreach to patients who have fallen out of care. \n3)\tPrenatal care: Erie OB/GYN, Family Medicine Providers, and Certified Nurse Midwives provide a full range of prenatal care consistent with American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) and other requirements.\n4)\tWell Woman Visits: Erie providers will offer a full range of preconception health and well-woman care including pelvic and breast exams, cervical cancer screening, review of menstrual and reproductive history, basic gynecological ultrasounds, and colposcopy.\n5)\tFamily Planning: Erie will provide a broad range of programs and services such as contraceptive access and education, counseling, examinations, assistance to achieve pregnancy, physical assessment, basic infertility services, STI testing and treatment, preconception health services, adolescent-friendly health services and vasectomies.\n6)\tOral Healthcare: Erie will provide preventative, prosthodontic, endodontic and emergency and periodontal services for pregnant patients at four of its locations.\n7)\tCase Management and WIC: Case managers will assist Erie\u2019s pregnant patients to find safe, secure shelter, enroll them in programs and provide counseling, health navigation, breastfeeding and nutrition support, and linkages to address social determinants of health.\n8)\tBehavioral health: Erie will offer behavioral health services to patients with low level to serious mental health concerns as well as monitor a registry of pregnant patients with symptoms of depression.\n9)\tSocial Determinants of Health. Erie\u2019s SDoH Care Coordinators will provide a range of support to help patients navigate the healthcare and social services landscape to overcome health related social need barriers including support like  getting access to food, filling out applications for rental assistance, accessing transportation and durable medical equipment, scheduling referrals, and getting connected to essential resources such as baby items and housing. \n10)\tPediatric Care.  Erie\u2019s pediatricians visit infants at the hospital post-delivery to ensure continuity of care at Erie.  Infants can also be enrolled as patients at Erie ensuring access to recommended immunizations and well child visits.",
