    "leader_title": "Chief Growth & Strategy Director",
    "leader_email": "sana.syed@imancentral.org",
    "full_time_staff": "103",
    "part_time_staff": "5",
    "volunteers": "60",
    "mission": "Established in 1997, the Inner-City Muslim Action Network (IMAN) is a community organization that fosters health, wellness and healing in the inner-city by organizing for social change, cultivating the arts, and operating a holistic health center. IMAN\u2019s work is a direct response to the prevalence of violence, poverty, social inequity, and health disparities within Chicago's South Side neighborhoods, specifically the Chicago Lawn, West Englewood, and Englewood communities.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "IMAN currently operates a Federally Qualified Health Center at the intersection of 63rd Street and California in Chicago Lawn. We provide holistic care services for both adults and children including, but not limited to, physical exams, cancer screenings, vaccinations, diabetes care, blood pressure management, women\u2019s health services, and more. Our Behavioral Health Clinic provides individual, group, family and couples therapy, case management services, and substance abuse counseling. These services, combined, demonstrate our collaborative, team-based care approach. To increase our capacity, we have developed the Health Center Expansion project.\nWhen complete, the expanded health center will be a three-story, 23,400 square foot building, intended to serve as a catalytic symbol of new development and investment along the 63rd St. corridor, in the eastern part of Chicago Lawn bordering Englewood. Expanding upon the newly renovated existing structure, this project will allow IMAN to significantly increase the Health Center\u2019s capacity, better equip its staff to execute a holistic approach to healthcare, and place all its operations under one roof to ensure efficiency and collaboration.\nThe new health center will allow IMAN to offer fully integrated primary care and behavioral health as well as robust wraparound services. Currently, IMAN\u2019s medical exam rooms and behavioral health rooms are located across the street from one another, with staff for both clinics scattered around the IMAN campus. This expansion will allow for greater synergy between the medical and behavioral health teams, which leads to greater cohesion between these different modalities of care for the benefit of IMAN\u2019s patients. The new facility will also include a critical community gathering space for local organizations and members of the broader community. \nIMAN\u2019s Federally Qualified Health Center is located in the South Side of Chicago. Our Health Center brings crucial affordable healthcare to medically-underserved neighborhoods of Chicago, containing approximately 1,058,365 service area residents, 50% of whom are living at or 200% below the Federal Poverty Level. Individuals in this service area, despite having significant socioeconomic needs and health disparities, have historically been left behind by healthcare initiatives. IMAN seeks to address this gap by providing substantial healthcare support and equity. \nThis service area has been designated as a Health Provider Shortage Area, Medically Underserved Area, and food desert. Residents experience significant health challenges related to chronic diseases and other health conditions, barriers accessing care, and disproportionate levels of community violence. Individuals from environments where trauma is common, like foster care, poverty, community violence and incarceration, require multifaceted wraparound services for true healing to take place, and those needs directly inform IMAN\u2019s holistic approach to patient care. By developing programs that address all aspects of wellness\u2014access to healthcare, behavioral health services, creative outlets, and spiritual spaces\u2014we bring wellness and healing to our communities.",
