    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Hope for Homes Day is a statewide online giving initiative led by La Casa Norte that brings together nonprofits across Illinois working to end homelessness. The primary focus of the campaign is to raise critical funds, increase donor engagement, and build public awareness around homelessness through collective action. The campaign specifically supports individuals and families who are experiencing or at risk of homelessness by mobilizing resources for the organizations that serve them.\n\nHeld annually, the campaign centers around a one-day online fundraising event\u2014taking place this year on July 17, 2025\u2014and is modeled after the GivingTuesday movement. Participating nonprofits receive access to matching grants, campaign materials, peer-to-peer fundraising tools, and ongoing technical assistance including bi-weekly office hours and strategic guidance led by La Casa Norte. The initiative is also amplified through media coverage and public recognition, including proclamations from Governor Pritzker, Mayor Johnson, and Cook County President Preckwinkle.\n\nIn its inaugural year, Hope for Homes Day raised over $153,000, fueled by $40,000 in matching gift sponsorships from the Chicago Community Trust and Knight Impact Partners. The campaign engaged 20 nonprofits, activated more than 520 donors, and launched 79 peer-to-peer fundraising efforts. With $30,000 in confirmed matching gifts for 2025, the initiative aims to grow its reach, involve more organizations, and continue driving impact in the movement to end homelessness.",
