    "mission": "Our mission is to empower immigrants and their families to become full participants in their community.\nOur vision is an integrated Lake County where everyone has access to opportunities and paths to success.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Since its founding in 2000, Mano a Mano (MaM) has operated as Lake County\u2019s only holistic and  comprehensive service provider for new immigrants arriving in the community. Founded by local village officials, MaM originally opened in a one-room store front on Main Street in Round Lake Park and served as an information center to orient newcomers to the community. Over time, the organization\u2019s founders and early leaders recognized that immigrant families needed additional direct services and support to effectively navigate their new community. In response, MaM established a new Round Lake Park office to include space for health education, immigration legal services, and classrooms for early childhood and adult education programming. Since 2016, the organization\u2019s footprint and services have expanded to include a satellite office in eastern Lake County and community-based, co-located offices in Wauconda, Mundelein, and Waukegan. The mission of MaM is to empower immigrants and their families living in Lake County, Illinois to become full participants in their community. The organization pursues its mission in the following ways: 1)  provides direct and supportive services, facilitates skill-building, and access to local community resources and opportunities; 2) serves as a hub for knowledge sharing on issues relevant to the immigrant community; 3) promotes best practice models of culturally competent services; 4) fosters leadership skills so clients can act to enhance their well being and the wellbeing of their community; and 5) influences policies and practices that affect immigrants and their families. MaM\u2019s vision is an integrated Lake County where everyone has opportunities and pathways to success. \nMano a Mano\u2019s Healthy Families, Successful Children, and Productive Parents programs directly align with Knight Impact Partners\u2019 priorities by advancing equity, fostering innovation in service delivery, and driving meaningful, long-term impact for immigrant and underserved families in Lake and McHenry Counties.\nEquity is at the core of Mano a Mano, as the organization is the only immigrant-serving organization in the area that provides linguistically and culturally responsive support to Latinx and immigrant families. Our staff is 97% Latinx and either directly impacted by immigration policies or have close family members who are\u2014ensuring programming is not only responsive but rooted in lived experience and community voice. We close equity gaps in access to healthcare, education, economic opportunity, and early childhood development by meeting families where they are and walking alongside them as trusted partners.\nInnovation drives our delivery model. In Healthy Families, we embed health promotion, mental wellness, and nutrition education into existing community events, including mobile health clinics and school-based partnerships. Through Successful Children, we integrate health literacy into kindergarten readiness and host bilingual/bi-cultural relevant literacy-based nutrition workshops. Productive Parents leverages ESL, GED, digital literacy, and workforce preparation to support parents' full participation in civic and economic life\u2014an intergenerational approach to systems change.\nTogether, these programs create a comprehensive, transformational wraparound model that supports family well-being at every stage\u2014empowering individuals to become healthier, more engaged, and economically secure. We have grown from serving 5,000 community members in 2019 to over 9,000 today, reflecting both the demand and the trust we've cultivated in our community. With support from Knight Impact Partners, we can continue to scale this work and replicate best practices in similarly underserved regions.",
