    "year_founded": "1983",
    "tax_id": "36-3265804",
    "contact_first_name": "Hilary",
    "contact_last_name": "Morreale",
    "contact_title": "Senior Institutional Giving Manager",
    "contact_email": "hmorreale@newmoms.org",
    "leader_first_name": "Laura",
    "leader_last_name": "Zumdahl",
    "leader_title": "President & CEO",
    "leader_email": "lzumdahl@newmoms.org",
    "full_time_staff": "60",
    "part_time_staff": "12",
    "volunteers": "250",
    "mission": "Mission: New Moms strengthens families by partnering with young moms as they progress toward housing stability, economic mobility, and family well-being. \n\nVision: New Moms envisions a future where every young family thrives.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Primary Focus: \nNew Moms\u2019 primary focus is addressing the needs of young moms and their children, who are experiencing poverty and homelessness in Chicagoland. We believe that motherhood is powerful\u2014using our Executive Skills Coaching approach, we serve ~350 families annually\u2014coaching young moms through our integrated housing, job training, and family support programs\u2014helping young moms to stabilize, set goals, and work toward lifelong self-sufficiency. \n\nTarget Population: \nNew Moms serves young moms (aged 24 & under) and their children (typically birth-5). Young moms come to us with big dreams, but they are limited by toxic stress and systemic barriers. Among participants, 75% are Black; 22% Latina; 2% White; 1% Other. 97% are experiencing extreme poverty, and most have no permanent home. Due to the challenges of single parenthood, ~50% have dropped out of school. 100% report trauma histories. Their grit & determination have carried them this far\u2014but their unstable situations limit their abilities to handle the small things and develop long-term habits that will lead to success. \nThe wellbeing of mothers and children are inextricably linked\u2014young children who grow up experiencing chronic poverty are much more likely to struggle behaviorally, socially, and academically. Our two-generational framework ensures that the needs of mother and child are addressed simultaneously.\nDespite the challenges they face, we serve young families at a critical time in their development\u2014in early childhood and late adolescence, the two periods during which our brains develop most rapidly. We capitalize on this, helping families to rapidly build skills, form healthy habits, and foster relationships that will yield lifelong stability.\n\nKey Activities: \nYoung moms typically come to us with three universal goals: to find stable housing, obtain permanent employment, and build a strong family. New Moms coaches young moms, decreasing barriers and opening possibilities, so families can work toward those goals.\nAll of New Moms\u2019 programs are delivered through an Executive Skills Coaching approach\u2014placing each young mom in the \u201cdriver\u2019s seat\u201d of her time at New Moms. We do not offer a prescribed service plan\u2014rather, each young mom determines her own goals and dreams for her family, and we help her to achieve those goals. \nUnique in the country, our services are delivered through our core programs, designed to work together or separately\u2014decreasing barriers for young moms while equipping them with critical skills and support.\nHousing: Young moms and children need stability to take the next steps forward. New Moms provides transitional and permanent supportive housing, where young moms can choose to engage with a family coach and set personal goals toward family well-being. We provide center-based housing for 40 families in Chicago and 18 families in Oak Park. Serves ~78 families annually. \nJob Training: Economic mobility is key to lasting change. New Moms offers a comprehensive paid job training program, providing individualized career planning; education re-enrollment support; 16 weeks of paid training and transitional jobs at our social enterprise candle company, Bright Endeavors; and permanent employment placement assistance. Serves ~100 young moms annually. \nFamily Support: New Moms ensures that young families have all they need to thrive. Our Family Support program offers a holistic set of services, including prenatal education, doulas, home visits, peer support groups, and other parenting resources, tools, and meaningful social connections. Serves ~220 families annually.\nNew Moms offers robust supports to ensure that families can thrive\u2014participants in all programs are eligible to receive academic and/or financial coaching, to help them progress toward their goals. And we offer in-house mental health supports for young moms and their kids\u2014addressing a serious need in our community, while helping two generations build resilience. \nIn addition to our direct services, we believe in sharing what we\u2019ve learned. New Moms trains and consults with peer organizations, interested in implementing our strengths-based Executive Skills Coaching framework, to improve participant outcomes and create equity-driven change.",
