    "volunteers": "6700",
    "mission": "Our mission is Nourishing Hope through food, mental health and social services so that all of our neighbors can thrive. \n\nOur vision is a city where all people have the resources needed for a dignified life.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Nourishing Hope provides over 200,000 food, mental health, and social services to our neighbors each year. We meet fundamental needs with dignity and respect to help our neighbors thrive. Through our five-year strategic plan, we prioritize serving people disproportionately affected by food-insecurity.  Our expansion in the coming years will focus on building trusted connections with those in vulnerable states of transition and in historically marginalized communities. To keep barriers as low as possible, we only ask that clients self-identify they are at or below the federal requirements to receive Emergency Food Assistance. \n\nWe serve people across the city through the programs outlined below:\n\nIn Person Markets: Our in-person pantries provide nutritious food for our neighbors at two locations. The Sheridan Market, located conveniently next to the Sheridan Red Line station provided food for over 52,000 visitors in our most recent fiscal year. Our second pantry, El Mercadito, is located in Humboldt Park. The partnership between Nourishing Hope and La Casa Norte served over 18,000 visitors last year. Each pantry offers a market-like experience where clients can shop for items that most fit their preferences. Giving our clients a choice in their groceries empowers them and creates healthier outcomes. To increase the accessibility for people who may have time constraints, we also offer express pick-up. \n\nOnline Market: Nourishing Hope\u2019s most innovative program, the Online Market, is Chicago\u2019s first and only online food pantry service. The Online Market enables our clients to quickly and conveniently pre-order free groceries each month using any device with internet access. Users have many food options to choose from \u2013 including frozen meats, canned goods, dairy products, and fresh produce \u2013 and most items are accompanied by a photo for easy ordering and to reduce language barriers. After choosing their groceries, they can select a convenient time and place to pick them up. If they would like, users can also request a social services appointment with Nourishing Hope as they complete their order. The Online Market enables households in our community to access groceries in a new way. Through the platform, working families, and other clients stretched for time, have a new ability to access our services. Since the program\u2019s inception in 2019, we have completed over 85,000 orders for our neighbors. \n\nHome Delivery: Last fiscal year, we delivered over 10,000 Home Delivery orders to older adults and people with disabilities across Chicago. Once enrolled, Home Delivery participants \u2013 many of whom prefer to communicate by telephone instead of email \u2013 receive a phone call from Nourishing Hope each month to confirm their grocery delivery for the following week and select the menu they would like to receive. The Home Delivery program is another example of our commitment to healthier outcomes. We offer a vegetarian option, and our regular menu includes low-sugar and low-sodium foods that combat diabetes or high blood pressure. In special cases, we offer a ready-to-eat menu for folks with more restrictive dietary needs or specific health problems.\n\nHealth and Hope: Nourishing Hope started Health and Hope, a pioneering service that provides groceries directly to hospital patients facing hunger, in 2017. The initiative was launched in the oncology department at Advocate Illinois Masonic Medical Center in the Lakeview neighborhood. After being screened for food insecurity, eligible cancer patients were offered shelf-stable groceries when checking out of the hospital to ensure that they had plenty of food to eat when they returned home. Health and Hope has grown to partner with other local organizations, and it delivered 60% more groceries in the past fiscal year than the year before. \n\nCase Management: Nourishing Hope stands at the ready, prepared to help our neighbors overcome a variety of barriers through our knowledgeable social services case management. We have two full-time care coordinators and one full-time housing case manager who use their strong skills and experience to help clients navigate challenges related to housing, financial assistance, employment support, healthcare, public benefits access, and services for families and children. In the past fiscal year, we provided almost 3,300 case management services for our neighbors. \n\nMental Wellness: Our growing mental wellness team is well-equipped to help people struggling with a wide variety of mental health conditions and challenges. We have six full-time, licensed clinical therapists and a rotating class of graduate-level student interns on our team. We offer therapy in English and Spanish, and each of our team members has expertise in different types of counseling. We provided over 3,000 completely free therapy sessions last fiscal year. As part of Chicago\u2019s network of trauma-informed centers of care, we provide private, in-person services at Sheridan Market in Lakeview, El Mercadito in Humboldt Park, our Headquarters in West Town, and virtually through a HIPAA-compliant platform. Using a trauma-informed lens, we center our mental health care on each individual\u2019s needs and goals.",
