    "public_private_split": "89% of Renaissance's FY 2025 organizational budget is from public sources, including federal, state, and local agencies and subcontracts from partnering nonprofits.\n\nSince 2023, Renaissance has made significant investments in its capacity to raise funding from private donors, adding personnel, vendors, and technology to accelerate growth.  Private philanthropy grew from $492,000 in FY 2023 to a projected $700,000 in FY 2025.  In FY 2024, the agency launched The Campaign for Renaissance to raise $1 million for investments in the organization's capacity to sustain recent programmatic growth; to date, the campaign has secured $188,000 in pledges and has multiple significant gifts pending.",
    "private_funding_sources": "For FY 2025, Renaissance's top three private donors are:\n\nCrown Family Philanthropies ($100,000)\nCuore e Mani Foundation ($100,000)\nPolk Bros. Foundation ($64,000)",
