    "mission": "The mission of The Resurrection Project (TRP) is to build trusting relationships to educate and propel individuals, immigrants and families to achieve their social and economic aspirations, stable homes and equitable participation in their community. The vision of TRP is that people will have the increased capacity to reach their goals and improve their socio-economic status.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "For 35 years, The Resurrection Project (TRP) has led affordable housing, financial empowerment, family wellness, and immigrant justice initiatives on Chicago\u2019s southwest side, supporting tens of thousands of individuals, immigrants, and families in achieving stable housing, economic mobility, and equitable participation in their communities.\n\nBased in Southwest Chicago, TRP primarily serves low- and moderate-income Latino individuals and families. Last year, 87% of TRP clients were Latino. Many are mixed status immigrant families. Most TRP clients or their parents emigrated from Mexico. All TRP services are available in English and Spanish. More than 80% of Full Circle Homes program clients are Latino and 40% are immigrants, utilizing Individual Taxpayer Identification Numbers (ITINs) to purchase homes.\n\nIn 1991, TRP purchased its first property and began to employ three interdependent strategies\u2014property management, real estate development, and financial services and education\u2014to help residents gain greater financial security and build wealth. Since then, TRP has grown to create and preserve $929 million in community wealth by building affordable housing and by helping residents attain and maintain homeownership.\n\nThrough its community development programs, TRP addresses the supply and demand sides of neighborhood housing markets. TRP develops affordable housing for renters and homebuyers, preserving and increasing the stock of high-quality affordable housing on Chicago\u2019s southwest side. TRP develops affordable rental housing to low-income renters earning up to 60% AMI ($71,940 for a family of four as of April 2025). Additionally, TRP develops single-family (1-4 unit) homes for low- to moderate-income buyers to purchase.\n\nTRP builds the supply of educated homeowners to purchase these homes through Full Circle Homes, TRP\u2019s comprehensive model for affordable homeownership. Services include:\n\nFinancial Education and Counseling: A HUD-approved housing counseling agency, TRP provides homebuyer education classes and one-on-one counseling for financial empowerment, home purchase, and housing stability.\n\nTRP Realty: Through TRP's nonprofit Real Estate brokerage, licensed real estate agents connect ready buyers to affordable homeownership opportunities.\n\nTRP Lending (CDFI): TRP\u2019s Community Development Financial Institution offers affordable lending products supporting home buyers and homeowners, including Down Payment Assistance, Second Mortgages for Home Purchase, and Home Improvement Loans.",
