    "mission": "Vision: Real Financial Security And Economic Opportunity For All Communities\n\nMission: The Inclusive Economy Lab partners with policymakers, community-based organizations and others to generate rigorous evidence that leads to greater financial security and real economic opportunity for communities harmed by disinvestment and segregation.",
    "program_name": "",
    "program_description": "Government policies and institutional structures have excluded many Americans \u2013 and especially the Black and Latinx communities \u2013 from opportunities for education, employment, and wealth creation. Building an inclusive economy - one that provides real economic opportunities for all communities \u2013 requires innovation, collaboration across sectors, and evidence about what works and what doesn\u2019t. Traditional research can take years, and the results often don\u2019t reach those who need the information most \u2013 the people living with and working on these issues.\n\nThe Inclusive Economy Lab solves this by working with policymakers, organizations, and communities to identify their most urgent and pressing challenges, co-generate evidence about what works, and translate that evidence into real policy change.  We focus on answering questions that are important to our partners, but bring the advanced research methods of a world-class university to bear on those questions. \n\nOur work spans housing, education, workforce development and safety net policy, allowing us to understand how inequities in one policy area (e.g., housing) can perpetuate challenges in another area (e.g., education). By building deep, long-term relationships with government agencies, we can better understand the goals and constraints facing policymakers and make practical recommendations. Our work is centered in Illinois, but our learnings have broad applicability nationwide.",
